that pushing forward with autonomous weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:44.720
would be disastrous for international security&nbsp;
and even domestic security. Wonderful. Richard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:52.160
Hi Emilia. Hi everybody. I'm Richard Moyes from&nbsp;
article 36 which is an NGO based in the UK. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.200
also coordinate the stop killer robots campaign&nbsp;
which is a partnership of non-governmental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.160
organizations more than 180 organizations&nbsp;
i think now who are concerned with this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.120
issue who are pushing for states to develop&nbsp;
an international legal treaty on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:13.360
issue. I suppose my background is really in the&nbsp;
world of weapons. I worked for like my clearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:18.800
organizations in the past and then i've been&nbsp;
working in the world of weapons policy and law so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:24.800
really coming at it not from the ai side but&nbsp;
from the side of thinking as a society about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:30.080
well frankly how we're allowed to kill each other&nbsp;
in in these international in these international&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:35.200
settings and recognizing I think Max used the&nbsp;
term drawing lines recognizing that when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:42.000
comes to how we we kill each other how we engage&nbsp;
in that you know very primitive practice in a way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.840
But there's a social recognition that we need to&nbsp;
