wars or other armed conflicts. That's not true.&nbsp;
Most people who were killed by weapons last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:36.560
year were not killed in Syria, Afghanistan,&nbsp;
Iraq, or Yemen. Yhey were killed in Mexico

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:48.240
why? Crime primarily. And it would be incredibly&nbsp;
naive to think that if you had these slaughterbots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:57.840
things as cheap and small as a smartphone&nbsp;
available in supermarkets or more likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:03.280
any arms black market right?... at&nbsp;
the same price as a kalashnikov rifle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:10.320
that these would that we wouldn't see exactly the&nbsp;
same use cases there. Just like most people in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:16.160
past were killed by weapons in civilian context,&nbsp;
they will even the future too. But now with these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:23.680
weapons instead that's the primary use case. And&nbsp;
do we really want to live in a future where anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:28.480
who for whatever reason wants to&nbsp;
kill anybody anonymously can do so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:35.600
for a very affordable price and not even&nbsp;
