00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:54.560
on this topic in particular? Sure, well first of&nbsp;
all I should say that I mean we totally see this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.280 --> 00:21:01.360
these sorts of risks and concerns as others have&nbsp;
mentioned security concerns, concerns for peace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:07.680
non-proliferation, conflict escalation, and&nbsp;
so on, I also take this opportunity perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:15.440
to say a little bit how the ICRC views or&nbsp;
understands autonomous weapons which is slightly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:21.520
different from some of the presentations that,&nbsp;
that we've already heard. So for us, what really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:27.680
sets autonomous weapons apart from other weapons&nbsp;
is that they select and apply force to targets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:33.200
without human intervention in the sense that&nbsp;
after their initial activation by a human being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:40.800
the system self initiates force application. It&nbsp;
is it is triggered in response to information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:46.480
from its environment received through sensors&nbsp;
and on the basis of a generalized target profile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:55.040
And so in our review this manner of functioning&nbsp;
is already a reality today. So this is not only,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:55.040 --> 00:22:03.440
this is not a future only concern. And, for&nbsp;
example, mines and sense of used weapons function&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:09.600
in this way certain so-called loitering munitions&nbsp;
or active protection systems and certain missile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:15.520
and rocket defense systems. And of course this&nbsp;
way your functioning could be applied to a wide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:22.400
variety of other weapons and munitions. And so&nbsp;
these can be relatively technically rudimentary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:29.360
or complex. And in our view they need not rely&nbsp;
on artificial intelligence or machine learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:38.320
techniques. But they may and they probably&nbsp;
increasingly will. So with that said, what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:38.320 --> 00:22:45.760
autonomous weapons then from this perspective have&nbsp;
in common is that the user does not choose and may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:52.640
not even know the specific target, the concrete&nbsp;
target that triggers a strike. And therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:58.640
doesn't know the precise timing or location&nbsp;
of the resulting force application. And this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:05.840
loss of human control and judgment in the use&nbsp;
of force brings with it fundamental ethical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:12.720
concerns that Richard has already&nbsp;
mentioned. In effect substituting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:12.720 --> 00:23:21.360
human decisions about life and death with sensors&nbsp;
software and machine processes and of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:28.480
it also brings particular challenges for users of&nbsp;
the weapons in terms of being able to anticipate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:34.800
and limit the effects of autonomous weapons&nbsp;
use. And that of course carries a risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:41.040
for those affected by armed conflict. Notably&nbsp;
civilians, but also soldiers or the gomba wounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:47.920
soldiers for example. And with it challenges&nbsp;
for compliance with the rules of international&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:54.640
humanitarian law, notably the rules that govern&nbsp;
the conduct of hostilities. So for example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:54.640 --> 00:24:02.560
there is a risk that an autonomous weapon that&nbsp;
is intended to strike military personnel carriers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:11.200
be triggered by a civilian car. And there is&nbsp;
also a risk that civilians and civilian objects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:17.600
may be harmed due to an autonomous weapon striking&nbsp;
in their vicinity. So, since autonomous weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:24.080
users do not choose the particular target and&nbsp;
time and location, the specific time and location&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:29.840
of force application, a critical question from a&nbsp;
humanitarian perspective and from the perspective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:37.200
of compliance with the law is: under what&nbsp;
conditions may uses of autonomous weapons be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:42.880
reasonably certain that an attack is not&nbsp;
directed against civilians and civilian objects?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:49.280
And that all feasible precautions are taken to&nbsp;
avoid and minimize harm to civilians? Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:56.320
civilians must be protected against the effects&nbsp;
of hostility. Civilians must not be targeted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:56.320 --> 00:25:08.000
war. And as so these these legal rules they demand&nbsp;
context-specific value judgments that do not lend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:16.960
themselves to being encoded in software processes.&nbsp;
And this specificity context dependency of legal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:22.160
assessment poses a major challenge to the legal&nbsp;
use of autonomous weapons from our perspective.&nbsp;&nbsp;

