day to get us towards that goal to get us towards&nbsp;
that treaty. Max? Let's see if I can inject some&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:48.400 --> 01:05:54.000
more optimism here at the end by zooming out a&nbsp;
little bit to the bigger picture. So you know here&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:54.000 --> 01:06:00.400
we are 13.8 billion years after our big bang,&nbsp;
sitting on this little spinning ball in space&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:01.600 --> 01:06:08.160
looking out and just into this amazing cosmos&nbsp;
that we've only become aware of the vastness of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:08.160 --> 01:06:19.040
pretty recently. Now why is it that 2021 is a much&nbsp;
nicer year to live in than 5000 years ago when&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:19.040 --> 01:06:26.080
the life expectancy was 30? Everything we love&nbsp;
about civilization is the product of technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:28.080 --> 01:06:34.240
and that's why I love thinking about&nbsp;
technology and working on technology, right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:35.280 --> 01:06:39.200
but it's important to not take technology as&nbsp;
our new religion and have this mantra oh you&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:39.200 --> 01:06:43.440
know more technology is automatically going to&nbsp;
be good because technology is not morally good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:43.440 --> 01:06:49.520
It's also not evil. It's just a tool that we&nbsp;
can use to do good or bad things and the key&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:50.800 --> 01:06:56.880
to get to where we are have gotten so far and&nbsp;
the key to an inspiring future is really to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:56.880 --> 01:07:03.920
make sure that it is we humans who control the&nbsp;
technology not the technology that controls us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:05.200 --> 01:07:10.240
And several of you pointed out that there's&nbsp;
no more ridiculous example of the latter than&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:10.240 --> 01:07:17.760
if you let the technology on its own go out and&nbsp;
decide you know who gets killed and who lives. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:25.360
more broadly for the optimism part, you know the&nbsp;
this is a much more fun and inspiring discussion&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:26.080 --> 01:07:30.400
the business about what to do with AI technology&nbsp;
than it is to talk about nuclear weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:31.200 --> 01:07:37.120
where you're just the two options are either we&nbsp;
destroy each other in a nuclear war or nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:37.120 --> 01:07:44.640
happens. There's no upside. Here there's an&nbsp;
enormous upside because our civilization has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:44.640 --> 01:07:49.280
built with human intelligence if we can amplify&nbsp;
this intelligence with artificial intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:51.600 --> 01:07:58.160
suddenly we're not going to be stumped by all&nbsp;
these things we're stumped by now. We will only&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:58.160 --> 01:08:05.600
be limited by the laws of physics. We can create&nbsp;
an almost unbelievably inspiring future where we&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:06.320 --> 01:08:10.640
figure out how to cure all the&nbsp;
diseases that are plaguing us today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:10.640 --> 01:08:18.560
we can stabilize our climate, we can enable&nbsp;
life to flourish, people living healthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:18.560 --> 01:08:23.600
meaningful prosperous lives. Not just for the&nbsp;
next election cycle, maybe for billions of years!&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:27.280
Maybe not even only on Earth but throughout&nbsp;
much of this amazing cosmos. You know&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:28.000 --> 01:08:34.160
it's this amazing upside that really really&nbsp;
makes it so important to ban lethal autonomous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:34.160 --> 01:08:40.720
weapons. The point is not to avoid bad&nbsp;
things. The point is to draw that line and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:42.400 --> 01:08:50.320
avoid doing these this tiny fraction of stupid&nbsp;
things that would derail us and make us squander&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:50.320 --> 01:08:56.240
this otherwise amazing opportunity that we have&nbsp;
and the more we can focus on the upside this truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:56.240 --> 01:09:02.080
inspiring future that we want to live in the more&nbsp;
likely it is that we will live in that future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

